<title>DUBAI: Oman Arab Bank lifts 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Oman Arab Bank lifts 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million Omani rials unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		 5.251	   vs     5.069</p>
<p> Net interest income    7.328	   vs     6.934</p>
<p> Other income	     0.307	   vs     0.041</p>
<p> Provisions		 0.041	   vs     0.022</p>
<p> Total assets	   203.631	   vs   182.375</p>
<p>Full Name: Oman Arab Bank SAOC.</p>
<p>Note - Jordan's Arab Bank owns 49 percent of Oman Arab Bank. The board recommended the distribution of 20 percent of paid-up capital as a dividend to shareholders for 1996 -- the same as for 1995. Two new branches were opened last year and the bank plans to open a branch at al-Ghalila in the next three months.</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom  9714-626990</p>
</text>
